---

<BaseLayout
  title="Pasaje de Matheu 4 glass arcade — first pint before Sunday kick-off | Dubliners"
  description="Sunday 8 Nov: O’Reilly’s at Pasaje de Matheu 4 is the covered glass arcade for a first pint before 15:00. Then hop to Espoz y Mina 7 and Four Corner Victoria 6 from 14:00. Weather cover, Maps, metres. Not a which-bar quiz."
  path={PATH}
  lang="en"
  hreflang={{ en: PATH, es: PATH_ES }}
  ogImage="/images/dubliners-screens-sol-1200.webp"
  extraJsonLd={[articleLd, faqLd]}
>
  <section class="hero hero-compact" data-show-until={SHOW_UNTIL}>
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumb current="Pasaje de Matheu 4: covered arcade, first pint before kick-off" schema />
      <h1>Pasaje de Matheu 4: covered glass arcade, first pint, then hop before Sunday kick-off</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Saturday is over. It is a November Sunday — rain or wind on the square is a reason to go <strong>under glass</strong>, not a reason to pick a personality of bar.
        <strong>Pasaje de Matheu 4</strong> is O’Reilly’s Restaurant Bar in the covered shopping arcade.
        Usual from 11:30. First pint before the 15:00 English kick-offs. Then hop out to Espoz y Mina 7 and to Four Corner on Victoria 6 (from 14:00, sports screens; not open before).
        Named listings: Dubliners What’s On only. Ask which screen.
      </p>
      <p class="small">En español: <a href={withBase(PATH_ES)} hreflang="es" lang="es">Pasaje de Matheu 4: galería acristalada, primera pinta, luego salto antes del saque</a></p>
      <FanWeekendCtas lang="en" findHref="/visit/" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>Weather cover and a first pint — not a which-bar quiz, not a two-door split</h2>
      <p>
        Other pages already pick a Sunday door by terrace vs screens, split a group at Espoz y Mina 7 (Premier 15:00 vs NFL later),
        or hop two streets for a last pint after Saturday’s derby.
        This page is only the <strong>covered first door before kick-off</strong>:
        November weather, glass roof, first pint at O’Reilly’s, then a short hop when Four Corner opens and the 15:00s start.
        We do not claim which match is on in the arcade.
      </p>

      <h2>Under glass from ~09:00 — even before 11:30</h2>
      <p>
        Pasaje de Matheu is a <strong>glass-roofed passage</strong> between Calle de Espoz y Mina and Calle de la Victoria.
        From about 09:00 it is <strong>about two and a half hours</strong> until O’Reilly’s usual 11:30, and <strong>about five hours</strong> until Four Corner 14:00.
        Pin <strong>Pasaje de Matheu 4</strong> now. Wait under the arcade if the door is still shut — do not camp Victoria 6 before 14:00.
      </p>
      <p>
        First pint in the passage (usual 11:30). Then hop:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Out onto Espoz y Mina 7</strong> — the street the arcade opens onto.
          Dubliners and O’Connell’s, same number, two doors. About <strong>1 min / 40–80 m</strong>. Both from 12:00 today (O’Connell’s usual Sunday 14:00).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Around to Victoria 6</strong> — Four Corner from 14:00 until late, sports screens, not open before.
          About <strong>2 min / 120–180 m</strong>. One hour of cover before the 15:00 Premier block.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Kick-off sits alongside — coordinate, do not substitute</h2>
      <p>
        Named on Dubliners <a href={withBase('/whats-on/')}>What’s On</a> (ask which screen — not every game on every screen):
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>15:00</strong> — Crystal Palace vs Liverpool · Sunderland vs Chelsea · Brighton vs Brentford · Ipswich Town vs Bournemouth</li>
        <li><strong>15:30</strong> — Bengals vs Falcons LIVE (NFL Madrid Game)</li>
        <li><strong>17:30</strong> — Manchester United vs Aston Villa</li>
        <li><strong>from 19:00</strong> — NFL evening / RedZone · <strong>21:00</strong> — Atlético vs Barcelona</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not copy that board onto O’Reilly’s, O’Connell’s or Four Corner. The arcade is the dry first pint; the hop is for screens after 12:00 / 14:00.
        Premier, NFL and Atleti sit alongside; coordinate, do not substitute.
      </p>

      <h2>Arcade, then the hop — addresses</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>O’Reilly’s Restaurant Bar — Pasaje de Matheu 4, 28012 Madrid.</strong>
          Covered glass arcade. Usual from 11:30. First pint before kick-off. Terrace restaurant-bar. We do not list its board.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.oreillys} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.oreillys} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Dubliners — Calle de Espoz y Mina 7, 28012 Madrid.</strong>
          ~1 min out of the arcade. Sunday from 12:00. Named Premier, NFL and Atleti listings on What’s On. Ask which screen.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.dubliners} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.dubliners} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>O’Connell’s — Calle de Espoz y Mina 7, 28012 Madrid</strong> (Maps listing: O’Connell St).
          The other door at the same number, ~1 min from the arcade. From 12:00 today (usual Sunday 14:00). Meeting point; we do not invent its board.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.oconnell} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.oconnell} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Four Corner — Calle de la Victoria 6, 28012 Madrid.</strong>
          Opens 14:00 until late · sports screens. Not open before 14:00. About 2 min from the arcade. Ask which game is on.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.fourCorner} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.fourCorner} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <OriginalFourBars lang="en" when="sunday" findHref="/visit/" />

      <h2>FAQ</h2>
      <dl class="faq">
        <dt><strong>November Sunday, first pint under cover before 15:00. Which door?</strong></dt>
        <dd>O’Reilly’s, Pasaje de Matheu 4 — glass arcade. Usual 11:30. Pin the passage now; wait under glass, not on Victoria 6. Four Corner from 14:00, sports screens, not before.</dd>
        <dt><strong>How far from Matheu 4 to Espoz y Mina 7 and Victoria 6?</strong></dt>
        <dd>Number 7 is ~1 min / 40–80 m (the street the arcade opens onto). Victoria 6 ~2 min / 120–180 m. Named listings: Dubliners What’s On only.</dd>
        <dt><strong>Does the arcade pint replace Premier, NFL or Atleti 21:00?</strong></dt>
        <dd>No. Coordinate. 15:00 Premier block, United 17:30, NFL 15:30 / from 19:00, Atleti 21:00 sit alongside after you hop. We do not assign a match to O’Reilly’s or Four Corner.</dd>
      </dl>

      <LinkHub
        heading="h2"
        groups={[
          {
            title: 'Covered arcade, first pint this Sunday',
            until: SHOW_UNTIL,
            items: [
              { href: '/', label: 'FIND US — Dubliners home' },
